[32m+[m[32m# Sprint 22 – Enterprise Query Engine[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Executive Summary[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSprint 22 introduced the Enterprise Query Engine for Andiny Atlas.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe sprint transformed investigation retrieval from a basic list-and-search capability into a structured, validated, ownership-aware and paginated query system suitable for enterprise applications and future frontend integration.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore Sprint 22, the platform could:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Create investigation cases.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Retrieve all investigation cases.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Retrieve one investigation case by its identifier.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Search cases using customer name or phone number.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Calculate investigation statistics.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThese capabilities were appropriate for the platform’s earlier development phase. However, returning an unrestricted list of records would not scale effectively when the number of investigations grows into thousands or millions.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSprint 22 therefore introduced:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Validated query models.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Generic pagination models.[m
[32m+[m[32m- SQL-level filtering.[m
[32m+[m[32m- SQL-level sorting.[m
[32m+[m[32m- SQL-level pagination.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Matching-record counting.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Ownership-aware investigation retrieval.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Pagination metadata.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The authenticated /support/my-cases endpoint.[m
[32m+[m[32m- An updated public response contract exposing investigation ownership.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Expanded repository and API test coverage.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe completed implementation preserves Andiny Atlas’s layered architecture:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mAPI Layer[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mValidated Query Models[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mService Layer[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mRepository Layer[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mSQLAlchemy[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mSQLite[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Sprint Objective[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTransform investigation retrieval into an enterprise-grade query capability by introducing reusable filtering, sorting, pagination and ownership-aware retrieval while preserving the existing layered architecture and automated test stability.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Engineering Motivation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mUp to Sprint 21, investigation retrieval was intentionally simple.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe application could return all cases or apply basic searches using customer name and phone number.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis design was sufficient while the dataset remained small. However, it introduced several limitations:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Collection responses were unbounded.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Large datasets could be loaded unnecessarily.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Pagination was unavailable.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Sorting choices were unavailable.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Ownership-aware retrieval required separate application logic.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Future filters would continuously expand repository method signatures.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Frontend applications would not receive pagination metadata.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Administrative dashboards would have limited querying capability.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- An enterprise platform must return only the records required by the client.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFiltering, sorting and pagination should occur inside the database rather than after loading complete collections into application memory.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSprint 22 addressed this requirement by introducing a reusable query architecture.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Architectural Decision[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe central architectural decision was to represent investigation retrieval requirements using a validated query object.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe previous repository search interface accepted individual optional values:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32msearch_cases([m
[32m+[m[32m    customer_name=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m    phone_number=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mContinuing this design would eventually create increasingly large method signatures:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32msearch_cases([m
[32m+[m[32m    customer_name=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m    phone_number=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m    created_by=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m    status=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m    start_date=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m    end_date=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m    region=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m    priority=None,[m
[32m+[m[32m)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSprint 22 introduced:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mquery_cases(query: CaseQuery)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis design allows future filtering options to be added by extending CaseQuery without repeatedly redesigning repository and service method signatures.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe approach provides:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Stable repository interfaces.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Centralized validation.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Improved OpenAPI documentation.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Easier frontend integration.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Reduced duplication.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Greater extensibility.[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Architecture Before Sprint 22[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBefore Sprint 22, collection retrieval followed this path:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mHTTP Request[m
