[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Repository Evolution[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Enterprise Query Engine was added to:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`app/repositories/case_repository.py`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe new method is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mquery_cases(query: CaseQuery)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIt returns:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mtuple[CaseCollection, int][m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe tuple contains:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInvestigation records for the requested page.[m
[32m+[m[32mTotal number of records matching the filters.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe repository intentionally does not create API pagination metadata.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThat responsibility belongs to the service layer.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## SQL-Level Filtering[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe repository supports filtering by:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mcustomer_name[m
[32m+[m[32mphone_number[m
[32m+[m[32mcreated_by[m
[32m+[m[32mstatus[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Customer-name comparison is case-insensitive.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe repository normalizes the supplied customer name using:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mstrip[m
[32m+[m[32mlower[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPhone number, ownership and status filters use exact matching.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen multiple filters are provided, they are combined.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExample:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mGET /support/cases?customer_name=Jane%20Doe&phone_number=08029876543&created_by=user-002&status=Escalated[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOnly cases matching every supplied condition are returned.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## SQL-Level Sorting[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mValidated sorting fields are mapped to SQLAlchemy model columns.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe requested sort order is applied as either:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mASC[m
[32m+[m[32mDESC[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA secondary ascending sort using case_id is also applied.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis creates deterministic ordering when several records share the same primary sort value.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor example, two cases may have identical timestamps. The secondary case_id ordering prevents records from changing positions between repeated requests.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## SQL Pagination[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe repository calculates offset using:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32moffset = (page - 1) × page_size[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExample:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mpage = 3[m
[32m+[m[32mpage_size = 20[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32moffset = (3 - 1) × 20[m
[32m+[m[32moffset = 40[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSQLAlchemy then applies:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mOFFSET 40[m
[32m+[m[32mLIMIT 20[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe database returns only the requested page.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis is more efficient than retrieving every matching investigation and slicing the collection inside Python.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Matching-Record Count[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPagination requires two related queries:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mData Query[m
[32m+[m[32mCount Query[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe data query returns records for the requested page.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe count query returns the total number of records matching the same filters.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPagination is not applied to the count query.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis ensures:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtotal_records[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mrepresents the complete filtered result set rather than only the records returned on the current page.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m---[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Service-Layer Integration[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe service implementation is located in:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`app/services/case_manager.py`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSprint 22 introduced:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mquery_cases(query: CaseQuery)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe service performs the following workflow:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mReceive CaseQuery[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mCall repository.query_cases()[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mReceive page records and total count[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mCalculate total_pages[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mBuild PaginationMetadata[m
[32m+[m[32m    │[m
[32m+[m[32m    ▼[m
[32m+[m[32mReturn PaginatedResponse[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTotal pages are calculated using:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mceil(total_records / page_size)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhen there are no matching records:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtotal_pages = 0[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe service layer owns this calculation because pagination metadata is application-response orchestration rather than database-access logic.[m
